<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- DELIBERATELY EMPTY.

	     A FREE personal Apple team cannot sign an app that declares either
	     Push Notifications (aps-environment) or Associated Domains
	     (universal links). Xcode refuses at provisioning time with:

	       "Personal development teams ... do not support the Associated
	        Domains and Push Notifications capabilities."

	     That refusal blocks the WHOLE device build, so declaring a
	     capability the account cannot hold makes the app impossible to
	     install at all — a much worse trade than not having push, which
	     nothing triggers yet anyway (no backend caller of send_push
	     exists, and the apple-app-site-association file is not served).

	     Both capabilities live in Empyralis-paid.entitlements. To turn
	     them on after enrolling in the paid Apple Developer Program, change
	     ONE line in project.yml:

	       CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS: Empyralis/Empyralis-paid.entitlements

	     Keeping the paid file present-but-unreferenced rather than deleting
	     it means the upgrade is a one-line switch instead of a rewrite, and
	     the capabilities we intend to hold stay reviewable in git. -->
</dict>
</plist>
